From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wheaney <42350981+wheaney@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 02 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] usb: raw-gadget: clear latched EP0 state on bus reset/disconnect

The Raw Gadget driver sets ep0_{in,out}_pending in gadget_setup() the
instant a SETUP arrives, before userspace responds, and only clears it
from gadget_ep0_complete().  When a control transfer is aborted on the
wire (the host issues a new SETUP or bus-resets mid-enumeration) no
completion runs, so the flag stays latched and gadget_setup() rejects
every subsequent SETUP with -EBUSY -- enumeration wedges permanently.

Hosts that pipeline/abort aggressively during speed negotiation (e.g.
macOS) trigger this reliably against the sunxi MUSB UDC.

Give the reset/disconnect gadget-driver callbacks bodies that clear the
latched EP0 state so the next enumeration starts clean, matching how a
real UDC forgets its EP0 stage across reset (musb_g_reset()/
musb_g_disconnect()).  Deliberately do NOT queue a RESET/DISCONNECT event
per IRQ: a single enumeration can produce many bus-reset IRQs, and one
event each overflows the fixed 16-slot event queue -> STATE_DEV_FAILED ->
every EVENT_FETCH returns -EINVAL and the userspace gadget dies.  Still
add the suspend/resume/reset/disconnect event types to the UAPI enum so
the kernel and userspace headers agree on their values.

Note: this must be paired with the sunxi_udc change that actually calls
usb_gadget_udc_reset() from its RESET IRQ; without that the callback is
never invoked.
---
 drivers/usb/gadget/legacy/raw_gadget.c   | 40 ++++++++++++++++++++++--
 include/uapi/linux/usb/raw_gadget.h      | 10 ++++++
 2 files changed, 48 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/legacy/raw_gadget.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/legacy/raw_gadget.c
@@ -366,11 +366,52 @@
 	return ret;
 }
 
-/* These are currently unused but present in case UDC driver requires them. */
-static void gadget_disconnect(struct usb_gadget *gadget) { }
+/*
+ * A bus reset or disconnect aborts any control transfer in flight.  Unlike a
+ * normal completion, no gadget_ep0_complete() runs for a transfer that was torn
+ * down on the wire, so ep0_{in,out}_pending stays latched.  Because
+ * gadget_setup() rejects every subsequent SETUP with -EBUSY while a request is
+ * "pending", a single aborted control transfer wedges enumeration permanently
+ * (seen with hosts that pipeline/abort aggressively during speed negotiation,
+ * e.g. macOS).  Clear the latched EP0 state here so the next enumeration attempt
+ * starts clean, mirroring how a real UDC forgets its EP0 stage across reset
+ * (see musb_g_reset()/musb_g_disconnect()).
+ *
+ * We deliberately do NOT queue a USB_RAW_EVENT_RESET/_DISCONNECT to userspace
+ * here.  A single enumeration can generate many bus-reset IRQs (some hosts, and
+ * a wedged/pipelining EP0, produce back-to-back SETUPEND+reset storms); queuing
+ * one event per IRQ overflows the fixed 16-slot event queue, which trips
+ * raw_queue_event()'s failure path and latches STATE_DEV_FAILED — after which
+ * every EVENT_FETCH returns -EINVAL and the userspace gadget dies.  Clearing the
+ * pending flags is the whole fix for the -EBUSY wedge; the userspace side does
+ * not need a per-reset notification (it manages its slot on CONNECT and at
+ * teardown), so keep this callback a pure, allocation-free state reset.
+ */
+static void gadget_forget_ep0_pending(struct usb_gadget *gadget)
+{
+	struct raw_dev *dev = get_gadget_data(gadget);
+	unsigned long flags;
+
+	if (!dev)
+		return;
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&dev->lock, flags);
+	dev->ep0_in_pending = false;
+	dev->ep0_out_pending = false;
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&dev->lock, flags);
+}
+
+static void gadget_disconnect(struct usb_gadget *gadget)
+{
+	gadget_forget_ep0_pending(gadget);
+}
+
 static void gadget_suspend(struct usb_gadget *gadget) { }
 static void gadget_resume(struct usb_gadget *gadget) { }
-static void gadget_reset(struct usb_gadget *gadget) { }
+
+static void gadget_reset(struct usb_gadget *gadget)
+{
+	gadget_forget_ep0_pending(gadget);
+}
 
 /*----------------------------------------------------------------------*/
 
--
--- a/include/uapi/linux/usb/raw_gadget.h
+++ b/include/uapi/linux/usb/raw_gadget.h
@@ -44,6 +44,16 @@
 	/* This event is queued when a new control request arrived to ep0. */
 	USB_RAW_EVENT_CONTROL = 2,
 
+	/*
+	 * These events are queued when the gadget driver is suspended,
+	 * resumed, reset, or disconnected. Note that some UDCs (e.g. dwc2)
+	 * report a disconnect event instead of a reset.
+	 */
+	USB_RAW_EVENT_SUSPEND = 3,
+	USB_RAW_EVENT_RESUME = 4,
+	USB_RAW_EVENT_RESET = 5,
+	USB_RAW_EVENT_DISCONNECT = 6,
+
 	/* The list might grow in the future. */
 };
 
-- 
